Subject: [PATCH] test(cli): compaction runs under ACP from providers.json
 settings (red first)

Test-only commit for fork patch 0012. Against the tag plus patches 0001-0011 an ACP
session builds no compaction, providers.json contextWindow is inert, and a full
1,000,000-token turn cannot shrink. The tests state the contract: the session config
takes settings.compaction {enabled, strategy, thresholdRatio}, on when the window is
known and off when it is a guess; a configured contextWindow reaches the budget of a
catalog model; thresholdRatio replaces the fixed 0.9 and a reported count exactly at
the threshold compacts for every estimate; a provider fault in the summary call ends
the turn with the structured error while any other summary failure falls back to
truncation; session/prompt reports the turn's compactions and settings in
_meta.harness; and a compacted transcript keeps every tool call paired with its result.

Rebased onto cli-v3.0.71 (test files taken from the rebased fork patch 0010, old number 0012).
